<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90816" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προωθέω</span></b> , aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προέωσα</span>, 
			contr.
		
		part.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρώσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Nat.Mul.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.206
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Strat.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Asin.</u>
				9
			</span></i>; imper. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρῶσον</span> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>:—<i>push forward, propel</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				84d
			</span></i> (metaph.), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				611b32
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Agatharch.
				5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				2p.59
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιαίως π. τινὰ ἐπί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chrysipp.Stoic.
					3.95
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. αὑτόν</span>
			<i>rush on</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				10.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> simply,
				<i>push</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπίσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					1.69
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.145
			</span></i>, Herod.
				Med.
			in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.Mus.</u>
				58.106
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			), <i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				46.27.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάτω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Nat.Mul.</u>
				</span></i>
			l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>thrust forward</i>, sens. obsc., <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
			</span></i> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be pushed forward</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.6.2
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ στῆθος ἔξω
			προεωθεῖτο</span>, in tetanus, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				<u>Or.</u>
				49(25).17
			</span></i>.</div>
